# Coding standards (non-negotiable)

## 1. NEVER use regex

No RegExp literals, `new RegExp`, or String/RegExp methods with patterns (`.match`, `.replace(/…/)`, `.split(/…/)`, `.test`, `.exec`, `.search`). Playwright/Vitest matchers with `/pattern/` are also forbidden. Shared ESLint (`packages/eslint-config`) bans regex literals/constructors and pattern-based string APIs — keep that in sync when this rule changes.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const ok = /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(hash);
url.replace(/\/$/, "");
page.getByRole("button", { name: /Copy/i });

// ✅ GOOD
function isSha256Hex(value: string): boolean {
  if (value.length !== 64) return false;
  for (const ch of value) {
    const c = ch.toLowerCase();
    if ((c < "0" || c > "9") && (c < "a" || c > "f")) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
url.endsWith("/") ? url.slice(0, -1) : url;
page.getByRole("button", { name: "Copy share text" });
```

Use `includes` / `startsWith` / `endsWith` / `indexOf` / `slice` / simple loops instead.

## 2. Always use Tailwind CSS

Style UI with Tailwind utility classes. Do not add CSS modules or large ad-hoc component CSS when utilities suffice. Theme tokens, keyframes, and page atmosphere in `global.css` may stay as the design system.

## 3. Code whitespace

Group related lines with blank lines. Do not reformat the whole repo blindly—apply when editing.

## 4. Comments for intent

Add short comments on non-obvious logic (why/intent). Skip noise on trivial lines. When touching a file for rules 1–4, improve comments there too.

## 5. File and component naming

- **Filenames**: dash-case (`generation-heuristic.ts`, `generation-features.ts`, `landing.spec.ts`).
- **UI components**: PascalCase for the file and the export (`VotePanel.tsx` → `export default function VotePanel`).
- Non-component modules (utils, server, i18n, tests) stay dash-case — never camelCase or PascalCase filenames.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
// generationHeuristic.ts
// generationFeatures.ts
// components/votePanel.tsx

// ✅ GOOD
// generation-heuristic.ts
// generation-features.ts
// components/VotePanel.tsx
```
